{% comment %}
  Renders one review card.

  Accepts:
  - rating: {Number} 1-5 (optional)
  - title: {String} headline (optional)
  - body: {String} review text (optional)
  - author: {String} reviewer name. Falls back to author_fallback (optional)
  - author_fallback: {String} used when the review has no author (optional)
  - product: {Object} referenced product, for live attribution (optional)
  - verified: {Boolean} shows the check icon (optional)
  - link_product: {Boolean} make the attribution a link (optional)
  - clone: {Boolean} this is a marquee duplicate. The wrapping set already
      carries aria-hidden, so nothing extra is needed here (optional)
  - shopify_attributes: {String} theme editor block attributes (optional)

  Renders nothing when there is neither a title nor a body, so an incomplete
  metaobject entry produces no broken card.
{% endcomment %}

{%- if title != blank or body != blank -%}
  {%- liquid
    assign stars = rating | round
    if stars > 5
      assign stars = 5
    endif
    assign who = author | default: author_fallback
  -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    role="listitem" rather than a real <li>: the marquee needs repeated sets
    wrapped in a container, and a <div> is not a legal child of <ul>. The set
    wrappers are display:contents, so each card is promoted to a direct child
    of the track's role="list" in the accessibility tree.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <article class="pl-card pl-glass-2 pl-rcard" role="listitem" {{ shopify_attributes }}>
    {%- if stars > 0 -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        The reference prints five glyphs regardless of the real value. Here the
        glyph count is the actual rating, and the exact value is stated in text
        so the meaning never depends on counting stars.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <span class="pl-stars" aria-hidden="true">
        {%- for i in (1..stars) -%}&#9733;{%- endfor -%}
      </span>
      <span class="pl-sr">{{ 'accessibility.star_reviews_info' | t: rating_value: rating, rating_max: 5 }}</span>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if title != blank -%}
      <p class="pl-rcard__title">{{ title | escape }}</p>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if body != blank -%}
      <p class="pl-rcard__body">{{ body }}</p>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if who != blank or product != blank -%}
      <p class="pl-rcard__who">
        {%- if verified -%}
          {%- render 'purelane-icon', icon: 'check' -%}
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- if who != blank -%}
          <b>{{ who | escape }}</b>
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- if product != blank -%}
          {%- comment -%}
            Attribution comes from the product reference, so renaming a product
            updates every review that mentions it.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <span>
            &middot;
            {%- if link_product -%}
              <a href="{{ product.url }}">{{ product.title | escape }}</a>
            {%- else -%}
              {{ product.title | escape }}
            {%- endif -%}
          </span>
        {%- endif -%}
      </p>
    {%- endif -%}
  </article>
{%- endif -%}
